## `marginal rate`

The marginal rate an earner pays.

```catala
scope MarginalRate:
  label marginal_rate_r0 definition marginal_rate
    equals
      0.05

  label marginal_rate_r1 exception marginal_rate_r2 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 900000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.5

  label marginal_rate_r2 exception marginal_rate_r3 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 800000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.45

  label marginal_rate_r3 exception marginal_rate_r4 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 700000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.4

  label marginal_rate_r4 exception marginal_rate_r5 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 600000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.35

  label marginal_rate_r5 exception marginal_rate_r6 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 500000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.3

  label marginal_rate_r6 exception marginal_rate_r7 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 400000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.25

  label marginal_rate_r7 exception marginal_rate_r8 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 300000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.2

  label marginal_rate_r8 exception marginal_rate_r9 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 200000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.15

  label marginal_rate_r9 exception marginal_rate_r0 definition marginal_rate
    under condition
      (e.income > 100000.0)
    consequence equals
      0.1
```

## Witness gates

### Witness gate for `marginal rate`

The rule of `marginal rate` is emitted as an exception ladder (Mode B). Each test scope below
calls that scope, not a copy of it, at one concrete input, and expects the value
L4's own evaluator computed there. The inputs are witnesses: each makes the 9
atomic conditions of the ladder take one combination of truth values. They are drawn
from a fixed candidate set (each number the conditions mention, one either side
of it, zero, both truth values, every constructor), and every combination some
candidate realises is tested at up to eight of the candidates that realise it.
So an edit to that rule that changes its answer at any of these inputs,
including one exactly at a number a condition compares with, fails `clerk test`
(R4, §8.4).

The atoms, as L4 writes them:

- `p_0` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 900000`
- `p_1` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 800000`
- `p_2` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 700000`
- `p_3` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 600000`
- `p_4` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 500000`
- `p_5` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 400000`
- `p_6` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 300000`
- `p_7` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 200000`
- `p_8` is `(e's income) GREATER THAN 100000`

- Witness 1 (FFFFFFFFF): `Earner OF 0`; L4 computes `0.05`.
- Witness 2 (FFFFFFFFF): `Earner OF 100000`; L4 computes `0.05`.
- Witness 3 (FFFFFFFFF): `Earner OF 99999`; L4 computes `0.05`.
- Witness 4 (FFFFFFFFT): `Earner OF 100001`; L4 computes `0.1`.
- Witness 5 (FFFFFFFFT): `Earner OF 200000`; L4 computes `0.1`.
- Witness 6 (FFFFFFFFT): `Earner OF 199999`; L4 computes `0.1`.
- Witness 7 (FFFFFFFTT): `Earner OF 200001`; L4 computes `0.15`.
- Witness 8 (FFFFFFFTT): `Earner OF 300000`; L4 computes `0.15`.
- Witness 9 (FFFFFFFTT): `Earner OF 299999`; L4 computes `0.15`.
- Witness 10 (FFFFFFTTT): `Earner OF 300001`; L4 computes `0.2`.
- Witness 11 (FFFFFFTTT): `Earner OF 400000`; L4 computes `0.2`.
- Witness 12 (FFFFFFTTT): `Earner OF 399999`; L4 computes `0.2`.
- Witness 13 (FFFFFTTTT): `Earner OF 400001`; L4 computes `0.25`.
- Witness 14 (FFFFFTTTT): `Earner OF 500000`; L4 computes `0.25`.
- Witness 15 (FFFFFTTTT): `Earner OF 499999`; L4 computes `0.25`.
- Witness 16 (FFFFTTTTT): `Earner OF 500001`; L4 computes `0.3`.
- Witness 17 (FFFFTTTTT): `Earner OF 600000`; L4 computes `0.3`.
- Witness 18 (FFFFTTTTT): `Earner OF 599999`; L4 computes `0.3`.
- Witness 19 (FFFTTTTTT): `Earner OF 600001`; L4 computes `0.35`.
- Witness 20 (FFFTTTTTT): `Earner OF 700000`; L4 computes `0.35`.
- Witness 21 (FFFTTTTTT): `Earner OF 699999`; L4 computes `0.35`.
- Witness 22 (FFTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 700001`; L4 computes `0.4`.
- Witness 23 (FFTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 800000`; L4 computes `0.4`.
- Witness 24 (FFTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 799999`; L4 computes `0.4`.
- Witness 25 (FTTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 800001`; L4 computes `0.45`.
- Witness 26 (FTTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 900000`; L4 computes `0.45`.
- Witness 27 (FTTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 899999`; L4 computes `0.45`.
- Witness 28 (TTTTTTTTT): `Earner OF 900001`; L4 computes `0.5`.

502 combinations were proved impossible by an SMT solver (no input realises them), and so are not tested: TFFFFFFFF, FTFFFFFFF, TTFFFFFFF, FFTFFFFFF, TFTFFFFFF, FTTFFFFFF, TTTFFFFFF, FFFTFFFFF, TFFTFFFFF, FTFTFFFFF, TTFTFFFFF, FFTTFFFFF, TFTTFFFFF, FTTTFFFFF, TTTTFFFFF, FFFFTFFFF, TFFFTFFFF, FTFFTFFFF, TTFFTFFFF, FFTFTFFFF, TFTFTFFFF, FTTFTFFFF, TTTFTFFFF, FFFTTFFFF, TFFTTFFFF, FTFTTFFFF, TTFTTFFFF, FFTTTFFFF, TFTTTFFFF, FTTTTFFFF, TTTTTFFFF, FFFFFTFFF, and 470 more.

**What this does and does not establish.** It checks the emitted rule's own text
against L4 at the inputs listed above. An edit that changes the answer only at
other inputs is not caught, and a combination the solver proved impossible is
not tested.

